{"key":"587ddacc60b1a770","source_file":"Potts Fl - Fu.json","source_id":50564,"source_url":"concordance-full-ppl-satur","term":"Full","headwords":["Full","Fulness"],"latin":["Satur","Saturitas"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Full"],"latin":["Satur"]},{"english":["Fulness"],"latin":["Saturitas"]}],"header_sentences":["See Satisfy."],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2220","subsection":"3"},"text":"That they were averse to the goods of charity, is signified by fulness of bread ().","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"3254","subsection":null},"text":"In a good old age, an old man and full (). Explained.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"4620","subsection":null},"text":"An old man and full of days () = what is new of life... (For) full of days = a full state.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"721","subsection":"6"},"text":"They who were of the Jewish Church are called full state, from the fact that they have truths in abundance.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"full-587dda","url":"/meta/potts/full-587dda/"}